body:
I'm running into a problem with `searchFunction` not respecting the pagination. When I create my instantsearch object I pass in 

```
            searchFunction: function (helper) {
               // helper.getPage() == correct page
                var query = helper.getQuery().query;
                if (query === '') {
                    // for blank search (starting) everything within 50 is valued the same on geo.
                    helper.setQueryParameter('aroundPrecision', 50 * metersInMile);
                } else {
                    // when a search term is added anything within 500 miles is valued the same on geo.
                    helper.setQueryParameter('aroundPrecision', 500 * metersInMile);
                }
                // helper.getPage() == 0
                helper.search();
            },
```

the pagination widget doesn't paginate the results.
```
            instantsearch.widgets.pagination({
                container: '#pagination-top',
                maxPages: 50,
                // default is to scroll to 'body', here we disable this behavior
                scrollTo: false
            })
```

If I remove `searchFunction` it will start working again. I'm wondering if I have to set all the parameters (search term, pagination page) if I use `setQueryParameter` once. If that is the case does that mean helper loses all incoming options when `setQueryParameter` is called?
